ame><surname>Palacin</surname><given-names>C</given-names></name><name><surname>Romera</surname><given-names>B</given-names></name><name><surname>Taub</surname><given-names>N</given-names></name><name><surname>Vollebergh</surname><given-names>WA</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Disability and quality of life impact of mental disorders in Europe: results from the European Study of the Epidemiology of Mental Disorders (ESEMeD) project</article-title><source>Acta Psychiatr Scand Suppl</source><year>2004</year><fpage>38</fpage><lpage>46</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">15128386</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B18"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Schnurr</surname><given-names>PP</given-names></name><name><surname>Hayes</surname><given-names>AF</given-names></name><name><surname>Lunney</surname><given-names>CA</given-names></name><name><surname>McFall</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name><name><surname>Uddo</surname><given-names>M</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Longitudinal analysis of the relationship between symptoms and quality of life in veterans treated for posttraumatic stress disorder</article-title><source>J Consult Clin Psychol</source><year>2006</year><volume>74</volume><fpage>707</fpage><lpage>713</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">16881778</pub-id><pub-id pub-id-type="doi">10.1037/0022-006X.74.4.707</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="B19"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Zatzick</surname><given-names>DF</given-names></name><name><surname>Marmar</surname><given-names>CR</given-names></name><name><surname>Weiss</surname><given-names>DS</given-names></name><name><surname>Browner</surname><given-names>WS</given-names></name><name><surname>Metzler</surname><given-names>TJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Golding</surname><given-names>JM</given-names></name><name><surname>Stewart</surname><given-names>A</giv